    "long_instructions": "## Countdown Timer\r\n\r\n**Goal**: Use a **for loop** to make the number count down from **10 to 0**. Each number should appear once per second.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Do This\r\n\r\n1. **Find where to write your loop** inside the `countdown()` function.\r\n\r\n2. Use a **for loop** that starts at **10** and ends at **0**, counting down by **1** each time.\r\n\r\n3. Inside your loop, use the loop variable to change the on-screen number.\r\n\r\n   **Syntax:**\r\n\r\n   ```js\r\n   count.textContent = num;\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n4. Use `setTimeout()` to delay each update so the numbers appear one after another.\r\n\r\n   * Hint: multiply your delay by how far the loop has counted down, for example:\r\n     `(start - num) * 1000`\r\n\r\n5. Make sure the countdown ends cleanly at **0**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n  <summary>Need help? Ask the AI Tutor.</summary>\r\n  \t<ol>\r\n      \t<li>\"How can I make my countdown change once per second?\"</li>\r\n      \t<li>\"Why do we multiply by (start - num) for the delay?\"</li>\r\n      \t<li>\"What does the loop variable control in this loop?\"</li>\r\n    </ol>\r\n</details>\r\n",
    "start_sources": {
      "folders": {
      },
      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n  <title>Countdown Timer</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\" />\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>Countdown Timer</h1>\n  <button id=\"runButton\">Start Countdown</button>\n\n  <div id=\"screen\">\n    <span id=\"count\">10</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
          "active": true,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "script.js",
          "language": "js",
          "contents": "const count = document.getElementById(\"count\");\nconst runButton = document.getElementById(\"runButton\");\n\nconst countdown = () => {\n\n\n\n};\n\nrunButton.addEventListener(\"click\", countdown);\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
